  "known_limits": [
    "Policy selection is explicit. Rust Copy/Clone/Drop traits do not infer native assignability, move/copy constructors or noexcept. Native move_if_noexcept selects the transfer callback in the caller policy; no automatic C++ trait dispatch is claimed.",
    "Callbacks return Rust values. Address-dependent placement constructors and C++ implicit user move hooks caused by language-level relocation are not modeled by these adapters.",
    "Unsafe reconstruction/direct callers must suspend automatic Drop ownership and repair or discard dead raw slots on unwind. Passing an ordinarily owned live slot that a later destructor visits after failed construction violates the documented precondition.",
    "Destructors must not unwind for native noexcept parity. Rust unwinding or process abort for violated destructor preconditions is outside the accepted domain.",
    "Generic existing Rust emplace_value still uses Rust value replacement. These explicit policies are not a blanket claim that every Rust T behaves like every C++ T.",
